# ---------------- BACK MATTER: GLOSSARY ----------------
GLOSSARY_TITLE = "Glossary of Terms"
GLOSSARY = [
 ("Right division","Correctly separating the Scriptures written to Israel (prophecy) from those written to the Body of Christ (the mystery), so each is applied to its own people and program (2 Timothy 2:15)."),
 ("Dispensation","A stewardship or administration — a way in which God administers His will in a given period. This present dispensation is the dispensation of the grace of God committed to Paul (Ephesians 3:2)."),
 ("The mystery","The truth kept secret in God from before the world and revealed through Paul: chiefly, Jew and Gentile made one Body in Christ, blessed with heavenly hope (Ephesians 3:3-9; Colossians 1:26-27)."),
 ("The Body of Christ","The church of this age — all believers baptized by one Spirit into one Body, of which Christ is the Head. Not a kingdom nation, but one new man (1 Corinthians 12:13; Ephesians 1:22-23)."),
 ("The prophetic program","God’s revealed dealings with Israel and the nations through Israel — the earthly kingdom hope foretold by the prophets “since the world began” (Acts 3:21)."),
 ("Circumcision / uncircumcision","Paul’s shorthand for Israel (the circumcision) and the Gentiles (the uncircumcision). Christ ministered to the circumcision; Paul was sent to the uncircumcision (Romans 15:8; Galatians 2:7)."),
 ("The kingdom","The promised earthly reign of Messiah over a restored Israel and the nations — the hope of the prophetic program, distinct from the heavenly calling of the Body."),
 ("The blessed hope","The Body’s expectation of being caught up to meet the Lord in the air (1 Thessalonians 4:16-18; Titus 2:13) — not the same event as Israel’s prophesied day of the LORD."),
 ("The gospel of grace","Paul’s gospel for today: that Christ died for our sins, was buried, and rose again; salvation by grace through faith, apart from works (1 Corinthians 15:1-4; Ephesians 2:8-9)."),
 ("The day of the LORD","The prophesied time of God’s judgment on the earth preceding the kingdom — a prophetic-program event, not the Body’s hope (2 Thessalonians 2; 2 Peter 3:10)."),
]

